  "body": "If the AS is marked down then for every event persisted we create a new transaction for that AS with a single event in it. When the AS comes back online Synapse will then send these transactions one at a time, which can mean that an AS can take a very very long time to catch up, even if its processing the events quickly. We should send transactions with multiple events instead (though not too many).\r\n\r\n(Split out from #8604)",
